cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Measuring the MCP Supply Chain: Eight Null Results and a Population
  That Is Not the Population
message: If you use this dataset or these results, please cite it as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Poddar
    given-names: Prachet
    email: prachetpoddar@gmail.com
    affiliation: University of California, Los Angeles
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-07
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
abstract: >-
  A measurement study of supply-chain risk in Model Context Protocol servers.
  Eight dimensions were tested against coverage-matched, size-adjusted and
  age-adjusted controls across 250 npm-distributed servers, 2,868 transitive
  dependencies, 400 published packages, 247 PyPI-distributed servers and the
  328-entry Docker MCP catalog. Seven results are null. The eighth survived
  every control and then dissolved under download weighting, falling from
  32.8% to 1.9%. The governing result is usage concentration: a Gini
  coefficient of 0.9611 on PyPI downloads, with one package taking 63.6% of
  installs, so the published population and the installed population are
  almost disjoint. The paper also documents two sampling errors that produced
  false positives in the authors' own data.
keywords:
  - software supply chain
  - Model Context Protocol
  - SBOM
  - null results
  - measurement study
  - sampling bias
